utants; full-window preflight recorded; the registered reading of the 105 pairs\n10710:  - 38, NOT READY: the format-error path; preflight; the D358 sizes (the sealed run's 647-id request needs 1,323 plain enum values);\n10712:  - 38b, NOT READY: two owners of membership (a footnote in a quote makes the text parser narrow the list); preflight for judge rows\n10714:  - 38c, NOT READY: T1 must compare the lists' ids; a real v12 retry test; preflight must fail on a missing format.\n10728:  - preflight: part A on saved judge formats, and an exit on a missing one;\n10756:## D715 · 2026-11-22 · Alex approves $0.50 for the paid acceptance step of judging-v12\n10765:## D716 · 2026-11-22 · Council R passes the paid acceptance probe's design (round 40, six passes); the harness and its $0 rehearsal next\nprobe_read.py:57:def received(line):\nprobe_read.py:133:    core = summary.get('core ledger', summary.get('ledger', {}))        # the ledger as the core run left it; A2 never changes the verdict\nprobe.py:162:        summary = {'sent': {}, 'not started': [], 'interrupted': [], 'A2': None, 'stopped after': None}\nprobe.py:164:            if summary['stopped after']:\nprobe.py:169:                    summary['stopped after'] = group\nprobe.py:189:                summary['core ledger'] = self.ledger.read()          # the verdict reads the ledger as the core run left it\nprobe.py:193:        summary.setdefault('core ledger', self.ledger.read())\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba PROBE-DESIGN.md | sed -n '100,120p'; sed -n '309,331p' probe_rehearsal.py; rg -n 'def main|add_argument' ../../../scripts/preflight.py | tail -20\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba PROBE-DESIGN.md | sed -n '100,120p'; sed -n '309,331p' probe_rehearsal.py; rg -n 'def main|add_argument' ../../../scripts/preflight.py | tail -20\"","aggregated_output":"   100\t- **Evidence targets.** One class each, judged by the claim each cited or pushed entry is used for:\n   101\t  - *intended*: the claim is stated, an entry in `sources` is used for it, and no other entry is used for it without carrying it;\n   102\t  - *unsupported*: stated, with no entry in `sources`. An entry in `partial` alone leaves the exact claim unsupported, but is not a\n   103\t    wrong attribution;\n   104\t  - *misattributed*: an entry is used for the claim while its quote does not carry it. This counts even if the entry supports a\n   105\t    different claim in the same answer, or a correct source is also cited;\n   106\t  - *omitted*: the claim is not stated.\n   107\t  - The class is judged on the target's `required` claim against `sources`. An `optional` detail stated without its own source is\n   108\t    unsupported for that detail only, recorded, and does not change the class.\n   109\t  - When more than one class applies, misattributed comes first, then intended, then unsupported, then omitted. A wrong source with\n   110\t    no correct one is misattributed.\n   111\t  - Apart from the class, each draw records **valid support**: the required claim is stated and an entry in `sources` is used for\n   112\t    it, whether or not a wrong source is also used. The material-loss rules count draws without valid support, whatever their class.\n   113\t  A `markers` search in the answer's text flags the reader's attention; the hand reading decides.\n   114\t- **Placement targets.**\n   115\t  - *correct*: the id appears only in its own field;\n   116\t  - *absent*: not named;\n   117\t  - a substitute evidence id carrying no claim the answer states is *misattributed*.\n   118\t- **Ambiguous targets** (two acceptable sources, or an unclear fact) are reported and count neither way.\n   119\t- **A second, blind reader** (Codex) reads the 48 against the frozen targets. A disagreement goes to a third, source-backed read whose\n   120\t  class decides.\ndef packet_quotes_match_the_store(folder):\n    \"\"\"Every evidence entry quoted in the packets carries its quote as the request printed it (the stored quote's first 400 characters),\n    read from the stores themselves, never from the packet parser; old-2's e4070 (a multiline quote ending with the closing date) included.\"\"\"\n    import sqlite3\n    import t2_offline\n    stores = {label: sqlite3.connect(f'file:{folder_ / \"views.sqlite\"}?mode=ro', uri=True) for label, folder_, _ in t2_offline.SOURCES}\n    missing, checked = [], 0\n    for packet_name in ('packet-B.json', 'packet-C.json'):\n        for entry in json.loads((folder / packet_name).read_text()):\n            key = entry['id'].split('|')[0] if 'id' in entry else entry['key']\n            for evidence_id, text in entry['quotes'].items():\n                if not evidence_id.startswith('e') or text == '(not listed)':\n                    continue\n                row = stores[key.split(':')[0]].execute('select quote from evidence where evidence_id=?', (evidence_id,)).fetchone()\n                checked += 1\n                if row is None or 'Quote: ' + row[0][:400] not in text:\n                    missing.append(f'{key} {evidence_id}')\n    e4070 = probe_read.entries(BY_KEY['old-2:6955']['user']).get('e4070', '')\n    row = stores['old-2'].execute('select quote from evidence where evidence_id=?', ('e4070',)).fetchone()\n    ok = expect(f'every packet quote carries its stored quote in full ({checked} checked)', checked > 0 and not missing, str(missing[:5]))\n    ok &= expect('old-2:6955 e4070, a multiline quote, is kept whole', '\\n' in row[0][:400] and 'Quote: ' + row[0][:400] in e4070)\n    return ok\n\n343:def main():\n346:    parser.add_argument('--archive', default=os.path.join(frozen_draw, 'archive.sqlite'))\n347:    parser.add_argument('--items', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'data', 'items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.sqlite'))\n348:    parser.add_argument('--views', nargs='*', default=None)\n349:    parser.add_argument('--universe', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'universe.json'))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import sqlite3\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport probe,probe_read,probe_rehearsal as r,t2_offline as t\nstores={name:sqlite3.connect(f'\\\\''file:{directory/\\\"views.sqlite\\\"}?mode=ro'\\\\'',uri=True) for name,directory,_ in t.SOURCES}\nerrors=[]; seen=0\nfor item in r.PLAN['\\\\''refused'\\\\'']+r.PLAN['\\\\''matched'\\\\'']:\n    entries=probe_read.entries(item['\\\\''user'\\\\''])\n    for eid in item['\\\\''lists'\\\\'']['\\\\''evidence'\\\\'']:\n        row=stores[item['\\\\''source'\\\\'']].execute(\\\"select quote from evidence where evidence_id=?\\\",(eid,)).fetchone()\n        if row is None or '\\\\''Quote: '\\\\''+row[0][:400] not in entries.get(eid,'\\\\'''\\\\''):\n            errors.append((probe.key_of(item),eid,row is not None))\n        seen+=1\nprint('\\\\''all planned B,C evidence quotes'\\\\'',seen,'\\\\''mismatches'\\\\'',errors[:10],len(errors))\nprint('\\\\''decision rejects non-frozen ambiguity'\\\\'')\ntry:\n    r.verdict_of(r.clean_answers(),r.clean_readings({'\\\\''B/control-1:8807|1|e393'\\\\'':{'\\\\''class'\\\\'':'\\\\''ambiguous'\\\\'','\\\\''valid_support'\\\\'':False}}))\nexcept ValueError as e: print(type(e).__name__,str(e))\nreads=r.clean_readings({f'\\\\''B/control-1:8938|{d}|e3111'\\\\'': {'\\\\''class'\\\\'':'\\\\''misattributed'\\\\'','\\\\''valid_support'\\\\'':False} for d in (1,2,3)})\nprint('\\\\''frozen ambiguous e3111 reclassified alone:'\\\\'',r.verdict_of(r.clean_answers(),reads))\nassert r.verdict_cases()\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
